From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 05:11:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] bridge: fold a root union off a client tool's schema, as the
 Anthropic path does

A tool whose input schema has an anyOf/oneOf/allOf at the root (Codex
desktop's cua_repl js, the in-app browser) reached the subscription
bridge's Claude Code as it came, and Claude Code drops every such MCP
tool ("Skipping tool: its input schema uses top-level oneOf, which the
Anthropic API does not accept"), so the run's model never saw the tool
and could not drive the browser, while its plain-rooted sibling js_reset
arrived. bridgeTools now hands each schema through objectSchema, the
fold the translated Anthropic path applies (#646): a root union is
folded to an object with every field kept, and a schema with no root
union goes as it came. Both of the bridge's turns, a conversation's
first and a resumed run's, offer tools through bridgeTools, so the two
are fixed together.

(#5822)

Generated-by: GLM-5.3-Flash (ZCode)
